  "producer_rules": [
    "Implement pure build_payload(rom_bytes, source_payload_raw, baseline_raw, contract_raw)->dict. No repository input/output and no publication API.",
    "Production build checks exact public contract SHA, ROM SHA/size, source_payload SHA/size and baseline raw SHA/size before parsing. Parent binds the other source identities and archive compressed identity.",
    "Expose derive_boundaries(rom, code_ranges, literal_ranges, literal_bindings) for hidden same-structure fixtures. Validate positive nonoverlapping code/literal ranges, finite regular align4 literal ranges; recompute gaps from full code/literal domains, not expected rows.",
    "Every positive code-end to adjacent align4 literal-start gap must be zero and have final Thumb unconditional B or BX. Decode signed B target or BX register. Fifth real BX r0 is indirect_pc_target, never a structured return. Conditional/fallthrough/nonzero/missing literal binding fails closed.",
    "Verify raw PC-relative LDR literal bindings: source halfword &F800==4800, PC alignment formula, consumed 4-byte ROM value. The parent independently proves complete instruction membership using existing upstream raw CFG verifier.",
    "Production derive rows must match expected_boundaries after deterministic IDs/kind/range SHA. Project every full gap through gapless baseline segments: all gap bytes unknown and no owners; copy left/right primary owner provenance only.",
    "Output schema/rom/source_inputs/baseline/summary/boundaries/promotion/scope. promotion.claims contains only id/kind/range/bytes_sha256 for the five gaps; claim_count=5 and promotion_bytes=10. No raw ROM bulk, no accepted or independent verifier success claim.",
    "TDD RED then GREEN; parameterized relocated synthetic B positive/negative and BX fixtures; zero gap/nonzero/fallthrough/conditional branch/range overlap/literal binding/known overlap/input mismatch failures. Tests may read fixed input files inside root for real integration.",
    "Only producer.py, test_producer.py and new logs/guard JSON below this packet may be written; CONTRACT.json read-only. No files outside packet, no Git mutations. Parent independently verifies and publishes later."
  ],
